From 84d7611e98063fbd3687fe90e5c529b4110bd137 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:06:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] sampling: K2-Horizon: empty-reply guard also holds EOG inside
 an unfinished Kimi-style tool-call opener

Live incident 2026-09-28 (official K2-Horizon-7B, opencode via LiteLLM, ctx ~28K,
effort low, 3 stalls in ~1 min): reasoning "\n<|tool_calls_section_begin|><|tool_call_begin|>"
then EOG (output 0, finish=stop), so the client ended the turn. The markers are not
vocab tokens (plain pieces), so they cannot be banned by id; the guard treated them
as real output and let EOG through.

Fix: the guard keeps a 27-char rolling tail of the generated text and masks EOG while
inside an unfinished Kimi opener (section_begin until section_end, or a bare call_begin
until call_end). Still out of the chain, cloned/reset with the sampler, never masks the
last candidate. common_sampler_init_empty_reply_guard is now exported for the test.

Evidence: not reproduced naturally in ~220 opencode-shaped replay runs (needs the real
opencode system prompt/tools). Forcing the opener into the stalled turn's prompt
(/completion, 40 samples, temp 0.8): 23/40 EOG immediately; with the guard state seeded
inside the opener 0/40 EOG, 25/40 native <ifm|tool_calls> call, 14/40 a Kimi-form call
left as reasoning text (still no parseable call), 1/40 other. Regression (after, stream
40 + non-stream 40 replay runs at ~24K ctx, plus 40 stream opencode-DB runs): 0 leaks,
0 stuck, 0 empty, 0 Kimi openers. ctest -L main 59/59 (58 + new test-empty-reply-guard),
-R split-balance passes.

